1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,200
<i>Help me. He's going to kill me.</i>

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:03,967
<i> What did mommy say?</i>

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,700
<i>I don't really understand
anymore.</i>

4
00:00:06,833 --> 00:00:07,667
<i> Mom, are you okay?</i>

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,733
<i> Don't pressure her.</i>

6
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:09,967
<i> Why are you interfering?</i>

7
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,600
<i>How dare you talk to me
like that?</i>

8
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:12,433
<i> Stop this!</i>

9
00:00:12,567 --> 00:00:14,267
<i>I'm worried about Ma'am Rebecca.</i>

10
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,833
<i>If Rebecca really has amnesia,
her memory must not return.</i>

11
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:19,367
<i> You think this could be her?</i>

12
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,667
<i> The video is too unclear.</i>

13
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,733
<i>If you want to go
see your friend, go.</i>

14
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:25,200
<i>Tell him we'll meet,
even Andrew will come too.</i>

15
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:26,033
<i> Okay, I'm on my way.</i>

16
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:27,100
<i> That's our target.</i>

17
00:00:27,233 --> 00:00:28,367
<i> Joey, wait a minute, okay?</i>

18
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,933
<i> - Andrew, what's that?
- Sorry, I thought there was...</i>

19
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:31,533
<i> Andrew, what's going on?</i>

20
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:53,200
Why, Joey? What happened?
[STAMMERS]

21
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:56,067
He's not answering, but it seems
something bad happened to him.

22
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,433
Come on, get in.

23
00:00:57,567 --> 00:00:58,900
Andrew?

24
00:00:59,033 --> 00:01:00,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

25
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:04,133
[CLACKING AND CLANKING]

26
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,033
[PETER GRUNTS]

27
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,700
- [THUDS]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

28
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:26,800
- [THUDS]
- [GRUNTING]

29
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:37,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

30
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:43,167
[GRUNTING]

31
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:50,300
[ENGINE WHIRRING]

32
00:01:50,433 --> 00:01:52,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

33
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:54,200
His car is here!

34
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:54,967
Where...

35
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:56,833
- Andrew!
- Andrew!

36
00:01:57,933 --> 00:01:59,200
Where is he!

37
00:02:01,467 --> 00:02:03,500
- Andrew!
- Andrew!

38
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:05,967
Andrew!

39
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,433
Let's split up!

40
00:02:10,567 --> 00:02:11,567
Be careful!

41
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:12,767
Be careful too!

42
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,633
- Andrew!
- Andrew!

43
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,433
What do you want? Money?

44
00:02:18,567 --> 00:02:19,900
I don't need your money.

45
00:02:20,567 --> 00:02:22,433
We came here for you.

46
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:23,700
Let's go!
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:32,000
- [THUDDING AND GRUNTING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:02:33,167 --> 00:02:34,233
Andrew!

49
00:02:36,233 --> 00:02:37,500
Andrew!

50
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,000
Andrew!

51
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,333
Andrew!

52
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:51,467
Bro, someone's here! Let's go!

53
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,767
Boss said just teach him
a lesson!

54
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,367
- Don't kill him! Come on!
- Andrew!

55
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:57,033
- Bro, let's go!
- Andrew!

56
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:01,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:02,567 --> 00:03:05,900
Andrew! Andrew!

58
00:03:06,033 --> 00:03:08,367
Help! Peter!

59
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,700
Peter, help!

60
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:10,900
Call...

61
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:12,833
Call an ambulance, quick!

62
00:03:12,967 --> 00:03:14,167
Andrew...

63
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:19,000
Andrew! Andrew! Andrew!

64
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:20,100
Andrew...

65
00:03:20,233 --> 00:03:27,133
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

66
00:03:29,567 --> 00:03:39,533
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,933
Get the car.

68
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:46,600
Where are we going, Boss?

69
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:49,067
We'll follow Jin Ho.

70
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:52,167
I'm going to deal with his
"so-called friend."

71
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:54,500
[PHONE CHIMES]

72
00:03:55,267 --> 00:04:02,833
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

73
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:13,467
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

74
00:04:15,367 --> 00:04:16,600
Yvette...

75
00:04:16,733 --> 00:04:18,800
Looks like Andrew won't be
coming back.

76
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:20,667
Maybe I should just go home.

77
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,233
It's up to you.

78
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:26,500
Sorry if Andrew left you.

79
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:28,867
You wasted your time.
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

80
00:04:29,033 --> 00:04:29,900
It's okay.

81
00:04:30,033 --> 00:04:32,600
At least I visited
Mommy Rebecca.

82
00:04:35,133 --> 00:04:37,000
Who are you again?

83
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,467
I'm Zoey.

84
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:49,667
I was your favorite
ex-girlfriend of Andrew's.

85
00:04:52,433 --> 00:04:54,233
His ex?

86
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:58,933
[PHONE RINGING]

87
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:01,600
Andrew, where are you?

88
00:05:02,233 --> 00:05:04,100
<i> This is Joey.</i>

89
00:05:04,233 --> 00:05:05,067
Joey?

90
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:08,033
<i>We need to take Andrew
to the hospital.</i>

91
00:05:08,167 --> 00:05:10,267
Why? What happened to Andrew?

92
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:14,800
[SIGHS]

94
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:16,900
Jin Ho!

95
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:18,733
Why are you still here?

96
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:20,867
I thought you were going
to meet your friend.

97
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,167
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]
It's cancelled.

98
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,033
No meeting tonight.

99
00:05:24,167 --> 00:05:33,100
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,000
[AMBULANCE SIREN BLARES]

101
00:05:35,133 --> 00:05:36,867
- Andrew!
- What happened to him?

102
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
We found him being attacked
by two men!

103
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:40,667
Who?

104
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:43,000
We didn't see their faces

105
00:05:43,133 --> 00:05:44,167
because they were wearing
helmets.

106
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:46,300
Before we could get there,
the two men left.

107
00:05:46,433 --> 00:05:47,733
Andrew, are you...

108
00:05:47,867 --> 00:05:48,667
Sir...

109
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,933
Sir, wake up.

110
00:05:50,067 --> 00:05:51,500
You'll be intubated
if you don't speak.

111
00:05:51,633 --> 00:05:52,667
- What's your name?
- Andrew...

112
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,933
Sir...

113
00:05:54,067 --> 00:05:56,533
- Andrew...
- Andrew!

114
00:05:58,367 --> 00:05:59,533
Sir, what's your name?

115
00:05:59,667 --> 00:06:01,100
Andrew, wake up.

116
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:02,567
Andrew.

117
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:03,700
So, his name is Andrew?

118
00:06:03,833 --> 00:06:05,100
Yes, it's Andrew, Doc.

119
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:07,700
Sorry.

120
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:09,000
You need to stay out.

121
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,467
Yvette...

122
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:32,133
Joey, maybe it's better
if we go home.

123
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:36,067
The way Zoey is looking at us,
it's like she'll eat us alive.

124
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,667
And your parents
might scold you.

125
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,467
Because we said
we'd just eat out.

126
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:49,233
Peter, if you want to go home,
then go.

127
00:06:50,267 --> 00:06:53,967
But I won't leave
until Andrew is okay.

128
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,300
But I won't leave you too.

129
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:59,667
And of course,
Andrew is our friend too.

130
00:07:02,333 --> 00:07:07,400
And it seems you two became
really close while I was away...

131
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:10,067
You cried so hard
over what happened to him.

132
00:07:11,033 --> 00:07:13,200
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

133
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,733
Peter, Andrew is important
to me.

134
00:07:19,033 --> 00:07:21,000
Due to everything
we've been through.

135
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,333
So, I hope he recovers.

136
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:32,833
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:37,100
His head wound isn't too deep,
Ma'am.

138
00:07:37,233 --> 00:07:40,167
But it still needs stitches.

139
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:42,600
The patient has many bruises.

140
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:48,433
But according to the CT scan,
there's no major problem.

141
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,967
No skull fracture, nothing else.

142
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,967
Do everything, Doc,
to make my brother better.

143
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:55,033
Of course, Ma'am.
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

144
00:07:55,167 --> 00:07:58,033
But we'll have to wait for him
to fully wake up.

145
00:07:58,167 --> 00:08:02,800
For now, we'll admit the patient
and then, we'll observe.

146
00:08:02,933 --> 00:08:04,133
Thank you.

147
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,767
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:11,567
Andrew...

149
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:16,767
Who did this to you?

150
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:25,867
They were wearing helmets,
so I didn't see their faces.

151
00:08:26,033 --> 00:08:30,233
You know, if you hadn't come,
we might have found Andrew dead.

152
00:08:30,367 --> 00:08:32,400
They beat him up so badly.

153
00:08:32,533 --> 00:08:34,433
Who could those animals be?

154
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,667
You know, I have an idea
who did this.

155
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,933
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

156
00:08:42,067 --> 00:08:43,200
Who?

157
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:46,500
Only one person knew
we were going there.

158
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:51,467
I'm sure he suspected
we'd confront him.

159
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:54,700
Jin Ho?

160
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,933
Joey, no, that's unlikely.

161
00:08:58,067 --> 00:09:01,600
It seems impossible.
Jin Ho wouldn't do this to us.

162
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:03,833
If not him, then who?

163
00:09:03,967 --> 00:09:05,700
Relax, Hon.

164
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:08,600
At least Andrew got medical
attention.

165
00:09:08,733 --> 00:09:10,200
He'll be okay.

166
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:12,700
I'm on my way to the hospital.

167
00:09:12,833 --> 00:09:14,300
I'll be with you soon.

168
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:17,500
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

169
00:09:17,633 --> 00:09:19,467
Your boys did well,

170
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:24,000
unlike the failed attempt
on Rebecca's life.

171
00:09:24,133 --> 00:09:25,433
[SCOFFS]

172
00:09:25,567 --> 00:09:27,833
You've had it
with your brother-in-law.

173
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,633
You didn't let him off the hook.

174
00:09:29,767 --> 00:09:31,733
He's too cocky.

175
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,200
That show-off learned
his lesson.

176
00:09:34,333 --> 00:09:36,500
And he's not the only one
I taught a lesson to

177
00:09:36,633 --> 00:09:37,933
with what I did.

178
00:09:38,067 --> 00:09:43,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

179
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:49,500
Come on, take me to my son,
please.

180
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,800
Did you get closer to Andrew?

181
00:09:51,933 --> 00:09:54,100
You don't even remember him
being your son,

182
00:09:54,233 --> 00:09:56,167
now your concern for him
is this much?

183
00:09:56,633 --> 00:10:00,033
Because he's always the one
watching over me here.

184
00:10:00,167 --> 00:10:01,900
I got used to him.

185
00:10:02,967 --> 00:10:04,433
And, Mom,

186
00:10:04,567 --> 00:10:09,533
Andrew is resting so let's visit
him tomorrow, okay?

187
00:10:09,667 --> 00:10:13,067
And you should rest too.
You also need to rest.

188
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,267
Please.

189
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,100
Okay.

190
00:10:21,733 --> 00:10:30,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

191
00:10:30,967 --> 00:10:34,900
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

192
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:38,167
Hon, maybe you should rest too.

193
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:41,133
I'm sure you're tired
from everything that happened.

194
00:10:41,267 --> 00:10:44,600
If you want,
I'll watch over mom.

195
00:10:45,733 --> 00:10:46,867
No, it's okay.

196
00:10:47,633 --> 00:10:50,933
Besides, I'll talk to the police
downstairs

197
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:53,133
about what happened to Andrew.

198
00:10:54,267 --> 00:10:59,500
Honestly, I have no idea
who did this to my brother.

199
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:03,300
We both know Andrew has done
many exposés,

200
00:11:03,433 --> 00:11:05,733
so lots of people are angry
with him.

201
00:11:05,867 --> 00:11:08,233
Maybe someone got offended
and retaliated.

202
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:11,633
What they did to Andrew
was too much.

203
00:11:11,767 --> 00:11:14,667
What? They were just going
to kill my brother?

204
00:11:14,800 --> 00:11:17,633
Well, that should serve
as a lesson to your brother.

205
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:23,567
He should be careful
who he crosses next time.

206
00:11:23,700 --> 00:11:29,067
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

207
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:37,667
After that,
they immediately left.

208
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:39,300
Why did they suddenly back out?

209
00:11:39,433 --> 00:11:41,300
I don't know either.

210
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:43,767
Do you have any idea
who would do this?

211
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,033
Ma'am Yvette! Excuse me.
Ma'am Yvette...

213
00:11:52,167 --> 00:11:53,133
Yvette,

214
00:11:53,267 --> 00:11:55,567
- how's Andrew?
- Has he woken up?

215
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:59,267
Well, not yet, but he's been
returned to the private room.

216
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,700
- Can I see him?
- Are visitors allowed?

217
00:12:00,833 --> 00:12:02,767
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:04,933
How dare you.

219
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:06,667
You have no right to see Andrew

220
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,733
because you're the reason
for all of this!

221
00:12:08,867 --> 00:12:09,967
What?

222
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,467
Andrew and I should have been
together,

223
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:14,100
but you called him
and brought him

224
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:17,067
to that godforsaken place
where he was attacked.

225
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:19,233
I didn't know that
would happen to him.

226
00:12:19,367 --> 00:12:20,233
Of course!

227
00:12:20,367 --> 00:12:22,300
Because you don't think
things through.

228
00:12:22,433 --> 00:12:23,600
You act on impulse,

229
00:12:23,733 --> 00:12:26,400
and then everyone around you
gets hurt!

230
00:12:26,533 --> 00:12:28,067
And where were you?

231
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,700
Why was Andrew
the only one beaten?

232
00:12:29,833 --> 00:12:32,567
Where were you when he was being
attacked?

233
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:35,367
Wait...

234
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:38,267
If you're going to fight,
just go home.

235
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:41,033
I can't handle any more stress,
okay?

236
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:43,267
And Andrew doesn't need this.

237
00:12:44,333 --> 00:12:46,133
You heard Yvette.

238
00:12:46,267 --> 00:12:47,633
Go, leave now!

239
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:49,067
Zoey...

240
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,567
you too.

241
00:12:52,633 --> 00:12:56,233
We've had enough for tonight,
okay? We don't deserve this.

242
00:12:56,367 --> 00:12:59,200
So, please go.

243
00:13:01,733 --> 00:13:03,800
Let's go, Joey. Let's go home.

244
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:09,433
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:13:11,333 --> 00:13:12,600
I'll go ahead.

246
00:13:13,033 --> 00:13:20,000
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:25,767
Andrew is still unconscious
when we left the hospital.

248
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:29,133
I'm really worried
about him now.

249
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:30,800
Now, you're worried?

250
00:13:30,933 --> 00:13:32,233
Didn't I tell you

251
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:34,433
not to interfere in my
investigation of Jin Ho?

252
00:13:35,433 --> 00:13:37,167
Why are you walking around
on your own?

253
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,867
What if you got dragged into it?

254
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,067
I was with Joey.

255
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,467
You too!

256
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:46,067
Instead of stopping her,
you allowed it.

257
00:13:46,667 --> 00:13:48,000
What if something happened
to my daughter?

258
00:13:48,133 --> 00:13:49,100
What would you do?

259
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:50,867
I'm sorry, Uncle Miguel.

260
00:13:52,567 --> 00:13:53,900
I'm sorry, Dad.

261
00:13:54,033 --> 00:13:55,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:13:56,267 --> 00:13:57,833
That's enough, Miguel.

263
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,900
Maybe now you've learned
your lesson?

264
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,633
It's my fault, Mom.

265
00:14:11,833 --> 00:14:14,567
Because of me, Andrew got hurt.

266
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,033
This wouldn't have happened
to him.

267
00:14:18,667 --> 00:14:28,567
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:14:40,333 --> 00:14:44,700
[PHONE KEYS CLICKING]

269
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:50,000
Your friends
must be really special

270
00:14:50,133 --> 00:14:51,800
for you to be this upset.

271
00:14:53,433 --> 00:14:54,533
Yeah.

272
00:14:54,667 --> 00:14:57,267
I was really looking forward
to seeing them.

273
00:14:58,933 --> 00:15:00,467
Special, indeed.

274
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:03,267
Who are these friends
of yours anyway?

275
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,967
Can you tell me more about them?

276
00:15:05,867 --> 00:15:09,000
I just met them
while I was looking for you.

277
00:15:10,967 --> 00:15:12,500
They were kind to me.

278
00:15:13,433 --> 00:15:17,767
I really felt that I was part
of their group.

279
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:19,767
<i>I'm not used to having a friend.</i>

280
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,333
<i> I'm more used to competing.</i>

281
00:15:21,467 --> 00:15:23,233
<i>But you don't have to prove
anything to me</i>

282
00:15:23,367 --> 00:15:24,567
<i> because you're my friend.</i>

283
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:26,600
<i> Jin Ho! Are you okay?</i>

284
00:15:26,733 --> 00:15:28,767
<i>I just wanted to give that
to you.</i>

285
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,867
<i> So that wherever you are,</i>

286
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,967
<i>you never forget that you have
friends.</i>

287
00:15:35,133 --> 00:15:38,700
But I ghosted them
when I found you.

288
00:15:39,533 --> 00:15:41,933
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

289
00:15:42,167 --> 00:15:43,333
That's it?

290
00:15:43,800 --> 00:15:46,300
Aren't you going to tell me
anything more important?

291
00:15:46,433 --> 00:15:49,700
Like their names
or where they're from?

292
00:15:50,067 --> 00:15:51,400
You won't be interested.

293
00:15:51,667 --> 00:15:56,100
They're just normal people,
not from our world.

294
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:00,167
[SIGHS]

295
00:16:01,733 --> 00:16:06,600
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

296
00:16:09,167 --> 00:16:11,000
<i> I should return this to you.</i>

297
00:16:11,133 --> 00:16:13,267
<i> Do you know this is for you?</i>

298
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,833
<i> Lucky you picked it up.</i>

299
00:16:14,967 --> 00:16:16,667
<i>I don't think luck is the word.</i>

300
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,733
<i>- What?
- Fate.</i>

301
00:16:18,867 --> 00:16:20,500
<i> It was destined...</i>

302
00:16:20,633 --> 00:16:22,333
<i> to end up with me.</i>

303
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:26,200
Dear...

304
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:29,167
Mom?

305
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,233
Why aren't you asleep yet?

306
00:16:33,767 --> 00:16:35,867
Because I'm still worried.

307
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:41,433
Do you want to say...

308
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:45,167
or tell me something
about Andrew?

309
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,567
What would I say, Mom?

310
00:16:49,667 --> 00:16:51,667
You know, my child...
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:16:52,033 --> 00:16:54,733
when your father
was courting me,

312
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,600
I played hard to get.

313
00:16:57,733 --> 00:17:01,167
I didn't admit to him
what I really felt.

314
00:17:02,233 --> 00:17:03,367
Really, Mom?

315
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,833
Yes.

316
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:10,533
Then one day he got hurt
on duty.

317
00:17:10,667 --> 00:17:12,200
That's when...

318
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:14,600
That's when I really realized
I loved him.

319
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:16,400
Because...

320
00:17:17,467 --> 00:17:20,900
it hurt me so much to see him
suffering.

321
00:17:21,733 --> 00:17:22,900
Sorry, Mom.

322
00:17:23,633 --> 00:17:27,667
I just don't understand
what I'm feeling.

323
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,967
It's my first time feeling this.

324
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,333
That's okay, dear.

325
00:17:33,933 --> 00:17:37,667
You don't have to be sure
right away.

326
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:41,100
What's important is,
always remember,

327
00:17:41,233 --> 00:17:44,667
whatever you want to say
or share...

328
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:49,400
I'm here, I'll listen to you.

329
00:17:49,567 --> 00:17:51,833
And I promise...

330
00:17:51,967 --> 00:17:54,100
I won't judge you.

331
00:17:55,933 --> 00:17:57,200
Thank you, Mom.

332
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:06,267
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL
MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:18:15,233 --> 00:18:16,667
[KNOCK ON THE DOOR]

334
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:24,367
Good morning, Yvette.

335
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,833
How is Andrew?

336
00:18:27,967 --> 00:18:31,567
He's stable, but still resting.

337
00:18:33,933 --> 00:18:40,667
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:43,600
Yvette...

339
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:47,300
I'm really sorry about
what happened last night.

340
00:18:48,367 --> 00:18:50,467
I know it's wrong
to make accusations,

341
00:18:52,067 --> 00:18:55,067
but I just feel bad
about what happened.

342
00:18:55,233 --> 00:18:56,667
I understand.

343
00:18:57,233 --> 00:18:58,900
Don't worry about it anymore.

344
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:04,267
He's just too important to me.

345
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,100
And you, his whole family.

346
00:19:09,667 --> 00:19:13,467
So, if you'll allow me, Yvette,
I'll watch over Andrew.

347
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:15,833
You already have too much
on your plate.

348
00:19:18,167 --> 00:19:19,200
Thank you.

349
00:19:20,233 --> 00:19:21,833
I feel...

350
00:19:21,967 --> 00:19:23,833
I feel better if...

351
00:19:23,967 --> 00:19:26,667
I personally know the one
watching over him.

352
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:30,800
And I've known you for years.

353
00:19:30,933 --> 00:19:32,133
And I think...

354
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:37,267
Andrew will be so happy to see
you here when he wakes up.

355
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:43,833
You being a law enforcer
makes me more confident

356
00:19:43,967 --> 00:19:46,200
for Andrew's safety.

357
00:19:47,633 --> 00:19:51,933
I'm just afraid the person who
did this to him might come back.

358
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:56,533
Yvette,
if you're worried about that,

359
00:19:57,567 --> 00:19:59,200
I have a proposal.

360
00:19:59,333 --> 00:20:02,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

361
00:20:02,967 --> 00:20:06,633
What if Zoey is inside?
You might end up fighting.

362
00:20:06,767 --> 00:20:09,500
I don't care what
that Zoey says.

363
00:20:09,633 --> 00:20:11,300
She can say whatever she wants.

364
00:20:11,433 --> 00:20:14,633
We're here to see Andrew.

365
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:19,000
Okay, but you promised.
Stay calm.

366
00:20:19,133 --> 00:20:20,433
Of course.

367
00:20:21,567 --> 00:20:22,933
That's the room.

368
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,700
Sir...
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:30,433
We're just visiting
Andrew Dizon.

370
00:20:30,567 --> 00:20:31,933
No visitors allowed.

371
00:20:33,133 --> 00:20:35,567
It's okay, Sir.
We're Andrew's friends.

372
00:20:36,533 --> 00:20:38,233
Is Ma'am Yvette there?

373
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:41,567
I'm Joey Delgado.
We're Andrew's friends.

374
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:43,767
We won't cause trouble.
We'll just visit him.

375
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,000
Sorry.

376
00:20:45,133 --> 00:20:48,967
Strict orders from Ma'am Zoey.
No one can enter.

377
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:52,200
Zoey? So, she's the one watching
Andrew?

378
00:20:53,267 --> 00:20:55,000
So, Zoey is inside?

379
00:20:55,133 --> 00:20:56,133
Peter...

380
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:59,267
Hey, Zoey, come out!

381
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,567
- Peter!
- Face us! Zoey!

382
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:04,067
Hey, Zoey, come out here! Zoey!

383
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,700
Don't cause trouble here.

384
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:07,567
[CLAMORING]
Zoey!

385
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:10,933
You are at the hospital.
Don't cause trouble!

386
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,433
Zoey, come out!

387
00:21:12,567 --> 00:21:14,133
He's so stubborn.

388
00:21:14,267 --> 00:21:15,900
I'm sure Joey is with him,

389
00:21:16,033 --> 00:21:18,567
that's why he's making
a scene outside.

390
00:21:23,367 --> 00:21:26,467
Andrew, don't worry.

391
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:29,067
I'll take care of it, okay?
Just rest.

392
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:32,600
I'll make sure that woman
won't bother you again.

393
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:38,567
[UNEASY MUSIC]

394
00:21:40,367 --> 00:21:42,633
- Zoey!
- Don't cause trouble here.

395
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,867
Zoey, come out!

396
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,100
- Sir.
- Peter!

397
00:21:49,633 --> 00:21:51,400
Go on, I'll handle this.

398
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:56,367
Let's talk calmly, no shouting.
Is that okay?

399
00:21:56,967 --> 00:21:58,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:21:58,233 --> 00:21:59,533
We don't have anything
to talk about.

401
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:01,033
We just want to visit Andrew.

402
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:03,633
Andrew's security is tight

403
00:22:03,767 --> 00:22:05,033
because someone attempted
to take his life.

404
00:22:05,167 --> 00:22:07,633
So, visitors must be limited.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:22:07,767 --> 00:22:11,333
Zoey, we don't want trouble.
We just want to check on Andrew.

406
00:22:11,467 --> 00:22:12,600
Is that it?

407
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,600
Well, he's fine.

408
00:22:14,733 --> 00:22:16,033
He's safe now.

409
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:19,400
He's resting to recover
and get his strength back.

410
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:23,200
Then why does it seem like you
don't want to show him to us?

411
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:25,300
Like you're hiding him.

412
00:22:25,433 --> 00:22:26,567
And you...

413
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:29,967
Why are you forcing yourself
to see Andrew?

414
00:22:30,367 --> 00:22:31,333
For what?

415
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:33,200
To get attention?

416
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,367
Come on, Joey.

417
00:22:37,267 --> 00:22:39,300
I know your strategy.

418
00:22:40,267 --> 00:22:43,567
You stick close to Andrew,
hoping he'll notice you.

419
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:47,067
You'll use every excuse
just to get into his orbit.

420
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:48,333
Why?

421
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,733
Because you like him, don't you?
Am I right?

422
00:22:52,767 --> 00:22:59,400
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

423
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:06,600
[GROANS]

424
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:14,333
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

425
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:16,233
Joey...

426
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,833
You're too obvious.

427
00:23:20,333 --> 00:23:21,800
It's embarrassing.

428
00:23:22,333 --> 00:23:25,500
You know what? I think Andrew
has noticed what you're doing,

429
00:23:26,367 --> 00:23:29,367
but he's just too much
of a gentleman to call you out.

430
00:23:30,533 --> 00:23:32,067
But believe me, Joey.

431
00:23:33,067 --> 00:23:38,033
There's no chance Andrew will
like an immature kid like you.

432
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:43,533
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

433
00:23:47,933 --> 00:23:49,167
<i>- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]</i>

434
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:52,067
<i> Help! Andrew!</i>

435
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:53,700
Joey?

436
00:23:53,833 --> 00:24:01,067
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

437
00:24:01,233 --> 00:24:06,000
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

438
00:24:06,133 --> 00:24:07,233
I'm telling you.

439
00:24:07,367 --> 00:24:09,467
Someone wants to hurt
or kill Andrew.

440
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:10,633
You know, I'll just think that

441
00:24:10,767 --> 00:24:13,500
I'm happy Andrew is awake
and recovering.

442
00:24:13,633 --> 00:24:17,567
Maybe it's time to move him
somewhere more peaceful.

443
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:19,333
This is our life, Jin Ho.

444
00:24:19,467 --> 00:24:20,767
You can't just walk away
from that.

445
00:24:20,900 --> 00:24:21,933
I have a plan.

446
00:24:22,067 --> 00:24:24,833
I'm thinking of the best thing
we can do.

447
00:24:24,967 --> 00:24:26,933
Peter, we won't be reckless
this time.

448
00:24:27,067 --> 00:24:27,967
Someone will help us.

449
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:29,400
[PHONE RINGING]
Jin Ho, we need your help.

450
00:24:29,567 --> 00:24:31,233
We don't know who else
we can trust.

451
00:24:31,367 --> 00:24:33,200
You know what?
I thought you were going to die

452
00:24:33,333 --> 00:24:34,500
when I held you?
